  <entry>
    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2312.15876v1</id>
    <title>On decomposition of neighborhood of a circular cone related to principal curvatures</title>
    <updated>2023-12-26T03:58:09Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.15876v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2312.15876v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>We give an alternative proof of a result on the uniform overlap of the algebraic sums of the sets arising from a decomposition of a neighborhood of a circular cone in $\Bbb R^3$. It is known that the uniform overlap result can be applied to make a unified approach for the proofs of a theorem on the maximal Bochner-Riesz operator on $\Bbb R^2$ and a theorem on the maximal spherical means on $\Bbb R^2$.</summary>
    <category term="math.CA" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
